        "block_02": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Delivered with its cofactors",
            "text": "100mg of pistachio extract per strip, carrying phytomelatonin in the form the plant made it."
          }
        },
        "block_03": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Nothing to clear at breakfast",
            "text": "No synthetic melatonin in the formula, and no escalating dose to keep it working on night thirty."
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "block_01",
        "block_02",
        "block_03"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "04 — The signal",
        "heading": "A plant signal, not a synthetic dose.",
        "body_1": "Melatonin is not a sedative. It is a timing cue — the molecule that tells your body which part of the day it is. Plants make the same compound, and pistachios are among the richest natural sources of it. That plant-derived form is phytomelatonin, and it arrives with the cofactors the nut carries rather than isolated in a lab.",
        "body_2": "The heaviness people associate with sleep aids is largely a dosing artefact: a cue delivered too strongly, or too late, is still in your system at seven in the morning. Research on low, well-timed doses finds circadian phase shifts without next-day grogginess.",
        "citation": "Cell Reports Medicine, 2023"
      }
    },
